	"note": "Motorcycles (D-083). Read by BikeRules (scripts/rules/bike_rules.gd). Per bike: gear_top_kmh = road speed at the redline in each gear (N is extra, gear 0); accel = drive m/s^2 in 1st at peak torque (higher gears divide it by their top speed ratio, so every gear pulls less); torque = [rpm fraction of redline, torque fraction] points (linear between); wheelie = how hard throttle lifts the front (x drive accel, vs gravity_pitch); lean_deg = most lean; brake = m/s^2 with S held; tank_l = fuel litres; engine = sound set (assets/audio/bike_engine/<engine>_low|mid|high.ogg); spawn_weight = how often it is the one found parked. shape = how the code builds the mesh (metres: wheelbase, wheel radius, seat height, tank, bars, fenders, fairing, exhaust). schemes = stock colour schemes [body, trim, frame], one picked when a bike spawns. tuning = shared rules: clutch_release_s (clutch fully out after letting go of Shift), stall_rpm_frac (of idle: below it with the clutch out in gear, the engine stalls), gravity_pitch / pitch_spring / rider_pitch / air_pitch (rad/s^2: what pulls the nose down - gravity x cos(pitch) + spring x pitch, so a steady throttle holds a steady wheelie - what leaning back/forward adds on the ground, and in the air), turn_grip (x the turn rate a lean gives at speed: 1 = real physics, 2 = half the turn radius), clutch_kick (extra wheelie per 1000 rpm of clutch slip), loop_deg / endo_deg (crash past these), land_pitch_deg / land_vy (a landing crashes past this pitch or this downward speed m/s), impact_mps (losing this much speed in one tick against something = crash), crash_damage_per_mps (above crash_safe_mps), fuel litres per minute at idle and at full throttle at the redline, gas_can_l per can, spawn chance per cell, fuel_spawn range (fraction of the tank), dismount_max_mps, zombie hits.",
